@format 1
@id media-loading.in-staged-workspace
@title In staged workspace
@section Media loading
@area In staged workspace
@entry staged-run
@summary Show the temporary workspace path used by staged processing: direct docket insertion selects a source, but the staged viewer is not command-active and rejects viewer loading.
@related media-loading.common.docket-insertion, media-loading.common.viewer-gate, media-loading.in-edit-tab, media-loading.in-audio-tab, media-loading.in-convert-tab, media-loading.in-merge-tab, media-loading.in-split-tab
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag staging

@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[staged-run] Cartographer staged-workspace execution <input>
- Construct a temporary PWorkspace for the planned layout and obtain its action/list surfaces @ workspace.PWorkspaceStageRun(...)
> staged-surface

[staged-surface] Staged Files surface available <decision>
- Require both an action surface and Files list before proceeding with the staged plan @ workspace.PWorkspaceStageRun(...)
? "Action and Files available" > staged-add
? "Required surface missing" > staged-rejected

[staged-add] Direct staged docket insertion <process>
- Pass the planned paths directly to LDocketPathsAdd with the planned batch and delivered=true; no PListMediaScan or PListPathsAdd occurs in PWorkspaceStageRun @ workspace.PWorkspaceStageRun(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
! Common / Docket insertion then synchronously selects the first added path and invokes whichever tab-specific PListPathChange adapter belongs to the staged layout.
> staged-viewer-result

[staged-rejected] Staged workspace cannot run <output>
= No docket insertion or media-loading attempt occurs.

[staged-viewer-result] Staged viewer command state <process>
- The temporary workspace is never attached as the active window workspace, so its viewer is not made command-active through PViewerCommandSet; a tab adapter that calls PViewerSourceOpen therefore returns at the common viewer gate @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerCommandSet(...)
! Audio can still run its local save/restore wrapper around that rejected call; other media-tab adapters simply return after the rejected PViewerSourceOpen. The staged action then proceeds with the planned processing and the temporary workspace is closed.
> staged-no-load

[staged-no-load] No staged preview load <output>
= Direct docket insertion occurred, but no backend media load starts from the temporary staged viewer because viewer commands are inactive.
